 ## Overview
-Semi-analytical volume rendering with trilinear interpolation is a direct volume ray casting technique for hexahedral cells that eliminates topological artifacts such as discontinuities and holes in isosurfaces by analytically determining optimal sampling points along the ray [S1]. It sets itself apart from standard trilinear interpolation [1531-trilinear-interpolation.md] by replacing uniform sampling with a piecewise-linear approximation over monotonic intervals defined by the analytical extrema of the reconstructed signal, ensuring no isovalue is missed [S1].
